    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, in-order enumeration of what happens on `POST /api/owners`, traced through `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`) and everything it calls.\n\n## Before the method body runs (framework layer)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires authority `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. (Only enforced when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; the \"security disabled\" profile does not enable method security, so this check is skipped there.)\n2. **Bean Validation on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`** \u2014 a failure throws `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 HTTP 400. Constraints:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`; `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern` `^[0-9]{4}$`\n   - `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid`\n\n## Inside the method (in order)\n\n3. **Idempotency replay (side-effect / short-circuit)** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key was already seen (in the in-memory `idempotencyKeyToOwnerId` map), it loads the original owner (`findOwnerById`), populates household size, and returns it with **200 OK** \u2014 no creation, skipping every check below.\n4. **Manual presence checks** \u2014 accumulates missing required fields into a list: `firstName`, `lastName`, then `address` (missing only if *both* structured `addressLine1` and flat `address` are blank), `city`, `telephone`. If any are missing \u2192 `InvalidRequestException` \u2192 400.\n5. **Address normalization (side-effect)** \u2014 normalizes `addressLine1/2` and flat `address`; composes a single `address` string (line1 [+ line2], or the flat address).\n\nThen, mapping the DTO to an `Owner` (`ownerMapper.toOwner`) and applying:\n\n6. **`deleted` set to `false`** (side-effect on entity).\n7. **`addressLine1`/`addressLine2`/`address` set** to the normalized/composed values (side-effect).\n8. **Telephone normalization + validation** \u2014 `normalizeTelephone`: strips separators, forces E.164 `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`, and enforces national length for `+61` (9 digits) / `+1` (10 digits). Invalid \u2192 `InvalidRequestException(\"telephone\")` \u2192 400. Normalized value stored (side-effect).\n9. **Email normalization + validation** \u2014 `normalizeEmail` (if present): validates the pattern, lower-cases it, and rejects disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Invalid \u2192 `InvalidRequestException(\"email\")` \u2192 400. Stored (side-effect).\n10. **Postcode validation** \u2014 `validatePostcode(city, postcode)` (if present): must be 4 digits and fall in the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Invalid \u2192 `InvalidRequestException(\"postcode\")` \u2192 400.\n11. **Registration-date not-in-future check** \u2014 if `registrationDate` is after today \u2192 `InvalidRequestException(\"registrationDate\")` \u2192 400.\n12. **Registration-date default (side-effect)** \u2014 if null, set to today.\n13. **Business-day roll (side-effect)** \u2014 `rollToBusinessDay` pushes the registration date off weekends/public holidays.\n14. **Daily-limit check** \u2014 counts owners already registered on that date; if `>= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY (100)` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` \u2192 **429**.\n15. **Bulk-signup warning flag (side-effect)** \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if today's count `> BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD (80)`.\n16. **City-capacity check** \u2014 if owners in that city `>= MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY (50)` \u2192 `CityCapacityException` \u2192 **409**.\n17. **Household id (side-effect)** \u2014 `generateHouseholdId(lastName, postcode)` stored as `householdId`.\n18. **Duplicate-household check** \u2014 if an existing non-deleted owner shares that `householdId`: allowed only if the request set `sharesHousehold=true` (marks `declaredHouseholdMember`); otherwise \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException` \u2192 **409**.\n19. **Duplicate-identity check** \u2014 computes `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`); if any non-deleted owner matches \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` \u2192 **409**.\n20. **Soft-duplicate detection (side-effect)** \u2014 unless the owner is a declared household member, `findPossibleDuplicate` runs; on a match sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf=<id>`, else `possibleDuplicate=false`.\n21. **Namesake count (side-effect)** \u2014 `namesakeCount` set from `countNamesakes(firstName, lastName)`.\n22. **Customer code (side-effect)** \u2014 `generateCustomerCode(owner)` stored (with dedup against existing owners).\n23. **Membership number (side-effect)** \u2014 `generateMembershipNumber(customerCode, registrationDate)` stored.\n24. **Persist (side-effect)** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` in its own `@Transactional`; DB insert, identity-generated id. (Note: the entity's own `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern` constraints on `address`, `city`, `telephone`, `firstName`, `lastName` are also enforced by the persistence provider here.)\n25. **Idempotency record (side-effect)** \u2014 if a key was supplied, `idempotencyKeyToOwnerId.put(key, owner.getId())` (in-memory map).\n26. **Household size (side-effect)** \u2014 `populateHouseholdSize(owner)` computes the transient `householdSize`.\n27. **Response mapping (side-effect)** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto` computes derived output fields (displayName, initials, membership points/level, locality, timezone, ageBand, Luhn check digit, salutation, links, etc.).\n28. **Audit log (side-effect)** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` writes id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber to the `AUDIT` logger.\n29. **Location header + 201 (side-effect)** \u2014 sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and returns **201 CREATED** with the `OwnerDto`.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- **There is no DB-level uniqueness** \u2014 no `@UniqueConstraint` or `unique=true`. All duplicate/household/identity enforcement is application-code only, and each `findAllOwners`/`saveOwner` is a *separate* transaction (the handler is not `@Transactional`), so the duplicate checks are racy under concurrency.\n- **No custom `ConstraintValidator` classes** and **no JPA lifecycle callbacks** (`@PrePersist` etc.) \u2014 the \"custom\" validation is all imperative helper methods in the controller.\n- **No application events** are published; the only non-DB side-effects are the in-memory idempotency map and the audit log line."
